    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for the Austin Waves is anchored by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, whose 83.85 score against Trevor Rogers makes him our highest-projected asset. He benefits significantly from park factors (+16%) and a favorable platoon matchup (+7%), positioning him as the primary engine for our counting stats. Following him, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Nasim Nunez** (64.14) represent our most efficient paths to stolen bases against Lucas Giolito; both receive a substantial boost from the pitcher\u2019s poor expected ERA (5.37), with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** specifically benefiting from a 14% platoon edge. **Gunnar Henderson** remains a must-start (77.96) despite the lack of a specific SP_xERA, as his base projection consistently carries the weight of our offense.\n\nThe most challenging decision today was the benching of **Josh Jung** (57.59), who barely missed the cut. While he projects as a solid contributor, the optimizer favored the higher platoon-adjusted ceilings of **Dominic Smith** and **Miguel Vargas**, despite their lower raw bases. Caution is warranted for the bottom half of the lineup: **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker** both face the formidable Zack Wheeler (2.86 xERA). While wind-out conditions offer a slight boost, both players face negative SP skill adjustments of 19%. **Liam Hicks** (50.94) and **Jackson Merrill** (53.18) also face stiff opposition, and since all lineups remain pending, the risk of late scratch-offs or lower-order shifts adds volatility to our daily efficiency targets. We will continue to prioritize speed and platoon alignment, but these elite-pitcher matchups represent the highest risk to our batting average floor today.",
